        "question_text": "Identify the $x$- and $y$-intercepts of the line shown.\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont}]\n\\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}\n\\draw[color=gridgrey,xstep=8mm,ystep=8mm] (-3,-1) grid (2,4);\n\\draw[<->,black] (-3.3,0)--(2.3,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[<->,black] (0,-1.3)--(0,4.3) node[above] {$y$};\n\\foreach \\v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2}{\\draw[black] (\\v,0.08)--(\\v,-0.08);\\node[below,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (\\v,-0.08) {$\\v$};}\n\\foreach \\v in {-1,1,2,3,4}{\\draw[black] (0.08,\\v)--(-0.08,\\v);\\node[left,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (-0.08,\\v) {$\\v$};}\n\\node[below right,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};\n\\draw[thick,<->,color=lineblue] (-1.9,-0.8)--(0.4,3.8);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
